# Android 16's MediaCodec needs the media resource manager (media.resource_manager) and refuses to
# create a codec without it ("Failed to get ResourceManagerService ... failed to initialize
# ResourceManager"). droidmedia's recorder, and with it hardware video recording, creates its encoder
# through MediaCodec. minimediaservice only fakes the resource manager up to Android 12, and the GSI
# keeps the stock mediaserver, which registers the real one, switched off (its service runs
# mediaserver_HYBRIS_DISABLED). Run the stock binary under a name of our own instead: it registers the
# resource manager and MediaPlayerService, which nothing else here registers.
#
# updatable: class main starts before the APEX linker configuration is loaded, and init keeps a
# service in the mount namespace it first started in. In that bootstrap namespace the statsd APEX's
# libstatspull.so cannot be found, so mediaserver never linked and init restarted it every few
# seconds. An updatable service is queued until the APEXes are ready and then starts in the default
# namespace.
service vendor.hybris-resmgr /system/bin/mediaserver
    class main
    user media
    group audio camera inet net_bt net_bt_admin net_bw_acct drmrpc mediadrm
    ioprio rt 4
    updatable
